WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.900
- [Instructor] In this
video, we're going to discuss

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:06.010
the naturalization process,
which noncitizens go through

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.900
in order to gain their US citizenship.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.020
Heads up that we won't be talking about

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:15.130
the eligibility requirements
that noncitizens must meet,

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.990
or any of the challenges
that they might face

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.290
along the path to naturalization.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.340
We'll cover those in other videos.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.880
This is just an overview of what happens

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.580
at each step in the process.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.950
If a noncitizen wants to start
the naturalization process,

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.210
the first step is for them to determine

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:37.730
if they are eligible
to become a US citizen.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.290
Then, they have to wait.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.510
If they are married to
a current US citizen,

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.180
they have to wait three years.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:50.150
If they are not, they
have to wait five years.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.720
During this time, many
immigrants take special classes

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.670
to prepare for citizenship.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:00.100
After the waiting period, if
they are at least 18 years old,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.670
and have been a resident

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.250
of the state where they intend to file

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.060
for at least three months,

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.957
they may file an Application
for Naturalization, an N-400.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.020
Once they've submitted their application,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.690
they must attend a biometrics appointment

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:19.770
to have their fingerprints
added to their records.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.550
Then they'll have to complete
an interview with an official

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:26.010
from US Citizenship and
Immigration Services

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:29.270
to ensure that they meet
the necessary requirements,

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:33.020
and to conduct the naturalization exam.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:37.210
The exam has two parts:
an English language test,

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:40.860
with questions about reading,
writing, and speaking English,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.120
and a civics test, with 10
questions on basic facts

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.500
about the history and
government of the United States.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.910
If the applicant gets six
of the 10 questions right,

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:55.690
they pass, and their
application is approved.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:58.530
The final step in the
naturalization process

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:02.660
is to attend a ceremony to
pledge an oath of allegiance.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:05.300
The noncitizen swears to be loyal

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.490
to the United States above all,

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:10.560
to obey the Constitution and other laws,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.660
and to perform military
or other duties if needed.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.300
Then, they sign a document,

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.600
and are declared a citizen
of the United States.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.840
And if they have any
children under the age of 18,

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.640
their children automatically become

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.110
naturalized citizens too.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.430
In the next video, we'll
go into more detail

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.703
about the eligibility
requirements for naturalization.

